  "scope": "Native namespace scenarios using exact production modules except a std mutex shim. The shim measures thread-local internal-mutex depth and the process allocator records alloc/alloc_zeroed, realloc and dealloc calls (including injected failed attempts) while depth is nonzero. Positive controls, poison/unwind recovery and independent thread depth are checked. Summary includes scenario setup between named operations, excluding instrumentation controls. This is a std host harness: no Arc atomic ordering proof, exhaustive scheduling proof, portable-spin allocator proof, real kernel allocator/IRQ proof or host ResourceDomain allocation claim. Controlled allocation failures cover only the initial ring and retirement Vec try_reserve_exact paths; no general OOM guarantee is inferred.",
